Chapter: GopPrograms
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites UI chapter Theme

 The launcher. The sidebar was a flat column of one button per app, so
 every app cost a row of the only column there is, and at 1024x768 it was
 full at thirteen. Groups here rather than rows there is what makes the
 fourteenth app free.

 An entry answers the SCANCODE its key would have produced. `desk-loop`
 already turns a scancode into a pane, so the launcher adds no second
 dispatch table -- the one nobody presses is the one that rots, which is
 the reason `GopCalc` does the same with its keypad. Adding an app here
 means adding it to `gpr-entries` and nothing else.

 We say:

Section: Geometry

  gpr-sel-cell : Integer = 0

Section: The Programs

 Each entry is a group name, a label, and the scancode the desk already
 answers for that pane. A row whose group repeats the row above it is
 drawn without a heading, so the group column is the sort order and the
 heading at once.

  GprEntry = record {
    ge-group : Text,
    ge-label : Text,
    ge-scan : Integer
  }

  gpr-entries : List GprEntry = [
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Accessories", ge-label = "Clock", ge-scan = 37 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Accessories", ge-label = "Calculator", ge-scan = 46 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Accessories", ge-label = "Calendar", ge-scan = 38 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Accessories", ge-label = "Aquarium", ge-scan = 16 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Productivity", ge-label = "Editor", ge-scan = 18 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Productivity", ge-label = "Issues", ge-scan = 23 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Productivity", ge-label = "Files", ge-scan = 33 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Productivity", ge-label = "Console", ge-scan = 20 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Productivity", ge-label = "Browser", ge-scan = 48 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Graphics", ge-label = "3D View", ge-scan = 4 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Graphics", ge-label = "Diffusion", ge-scan = 32 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Settings", ge-label = "Appearance", ge-scan = 30 },
    GprEntry { ge-group = "Settings", ge-label = "System Info", ge-scan = 50 }
  ]

  gpr-count : Integer
  gpr-count = list-length gpr-entries

  gpr-at : Integer -> GprEntry
  gpr-at (i) = list-at gpr-entries i

Section: State

  gpr-sel : Integer -> Integer
  gpr-sel (ps) = peek-32 ps gpr-sel-cell

  gpr-set-sel : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gpr-set-sel (ps) (i) =
    poke-32 ps gpr-sel-cell (if i < 0 then 0 else if i >= gpr-count then gpr-count - 1 else i)

  gpr-ensure : Integer -> Integer
  gpr-ensure (ps) = gpr-set-sel ps (gpr-sel ps)

Section: The Tree

 A heading is drawn only when the group changes, so the first row of each
 group carries it and the rest do not.

  gpr-heads : Integer -> Boolean
  gpr-heads (i) =
    if i <= 0 then True
    else (gpr-at i).ge-group /= (gpr-at (i - 1)).ge-group

  gpr-mark : Integer, Integer -> Text
  gpr-mark (i) (sel) = if i == sel then "> " else "  "

  gpr-key-name : Integer -> Text
  gpr-key-name (sc) =
    if sc == 20 then "t"
    else if sc == 18 then "e"
    else if sc == 33 then "f"
    else if sc == 4 then "3"
    else if sc == 16 then "q"
    else if sc == 32 then "d"
    else if sc == 48 then "b"
    else if sc == 23 then "i"
    else if sc == 38 then "l"
    else if sc == 46 then "c"
    else if sc == 50 then "m"
    else if sc == 30 then "a"
    else if sc == 37 then "k"
    else "?"

  gpr-row : Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  gpr-row (i) (sel) =
    let e = gpr-at i
    in widget-set-min (widget-button ("gpr-" & e.ge-label) (gpr-mark i sel & e.ge-label & "   (" & gpr-key-name (e.ge-scan) & ")")) 0 22

 Two columns, not one. Nothing clips a widget panel to its box, so a
 single column of sixteen rows drew straight through the help line and
 the taskbar below it -- measured on the glass, not feared. Splitting the
 groups across columns is also what a program manager looks like, so the
 shape that fits is the shape that was wanted.

 `gpr-split` is an ENTRY index and must land on a group boundary, or the
 group whose rows it cuts loses its heading in the second column.

  gpr-split : Integer = 9

  gpr-rows : Integer, Integer, Integer, List WidgetNode -> List WidgetNode
  gpr-rows (i) (stop) (sel) (acc) =
    if i >= stop then acc
    else let acc1 = if gpr-heads i then list-push acc (widget-set-min (widget-label ("gpr-h-" & (gpr-at i).ge-group) ((gpr-at i).ge-group)) 0 20) else acc
    in gpr-rows (i + 1) stop sel (list-push acc1 (gpr-row i sel))

  gpr-tree : Integer -> WidgetNode
  gpr-tree (ps) =
    let sel = gpr-sel ps
    in let left = widget-panel "gpr-left" DirColumn 2 (gpr-rows 0 gpr-split sel [])
    in let right = widget-panel "gpr-right" DirColumn 2 (gpr-rows gpr-split gpr-count sel [])
    in let cols = widget-panel "gpr-cols" DirRow 8 [widget-set-flex left 1, widget-set-flex right 1]
    in let help = widget-set-min (widget-label "gpr-help" "up/down choose   Enter opens   Esc returns") 0 20
    in widget-panel "gpr-pane" DirColumn 6 [widget-set-flex cols 1, help]

Section: Keys

 The answer is a scancode the desk already dispatches, or 0 for "nothing
 happened". Escape is the caller's business and is not handled here.

  gpr-key : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gpr-key (ps) (sc) =
    if sc == 72 then let d = gpr-set-sel ps (gpr-sel ps - 1) in 0
    else if sc == 80 then let d = gpr-set-sel ps (gpr-sel ps + 1) in 0
    else if sc == 28 then (gpr-at (gpr-sel ps)).ge-scan
    else 0

 A clicked row answers the same scancode its Enter would have, and the id
 carries the label because that is what the widget was built with.

  gpr-id-scan : Text, Integer -> Integer
  gpr-id-scan (id) (i) =
    if i >= gpr-count then 0
    else if id == ("gpr-" & (gpr-at i).ge-label) then (gpr-at i).ge-scan
    else gpr-id-scan id (i + 1)

